Computation issues to watch for
Students often make mistakes by:

ignoring the lower and upper index of a summation;
confusing \(\sum X^2\) with \((\sum X)^2\);
multiplying \(\sum X\) and \(\sum Y\) when the expression actually requires \(\sum XY\);
forgetting that a constant inside a summation is applied to every included score;
skipping parentheses;
calculating cumulative frequencies incorrectly;
forgetting that proportions must sum to 1.00;
forgetting that percentages must sum to 100%;
drawing histogram bars with heights that do not match the frequency table.

